// guid_no_include.tk -- docs/specs/guid.md § 11: the include is part of the
// surface. Every row names a symbol that lives in `lib/guid.tk`, so a program
// that wrote the type word without it is told which file it forgot instead of
// reaching the core's own `call to unknown function` two phases later
// (teko_prim.tk's `tk_prim_need_include`).
//
// D76: the wording gained its quotes. The include COLUMN was bare for `Guid`
// and pre-quoted for `TimeSpan`/`DateTime`/`DateOnly`/`TimeOnly`
// (`tk_time_include()`), and a `DateTimeOffset` registered under the second
// convention and read by `teko_wide.tk`'s own quoting would have printed
// `include ""time.tk""`. The column is bare everywhere now and one place
// (`tk_prim_inc_q`) quotes it, which is what moves this one wording.
//
// expect-refuse: teko: Guid needs #include "guid.tk" before it is used
// expect-refuse-line: 20

#include "rt.tk"

i64 main() {
    Guid g = Guid.Empty;
    return 0;
}
